 "issue": 2472,
 "issue_title": "Bug: ArFrame.to_dict leaks raw TypeError for unhashable orient values",
 "issue_body": "## Environment / context\n- Repository: `im-anishraj/arnio`\n- Tested against current source on `main` (`78d5ef1e5c7b3af48913a97ae1a02382139532f2`)\n- Python: 3.13.9 in local QA virtualenv\n- Affected API: `ArFrame.to_dict(orient=...)`\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n```python\nimport arnio as ar\n\nframe = ar.from_dict({\"a\": [1, 2], \"b\": [\"x\", \"y\"]})\n\nframe.to_dict(orient=[\"list\"])\nframe.to_dict(orient={\"mode\": \"list\"})\n```\n\n## Expected result\nInvalid `orient` inputs should be validated consistently and produce the same public API error as unsupported string values, for example:\n\n```text\nValueError: orient must be one of: list, records, split\n```\n\nor a clear `TypeError` explaining that `orient` must be a string.\n\n## Actual result\nUnhashable values leak raw Python errors before Arnio validation:\n\n```text\nframe.to_dict(orient=[\"list\"]) -> TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'\nframe.to_dict(orient={\"mode\": \"list\"}) -> TypeError: unhashable type: 'dict'\n```\n\nOther invalid but hashable values (`None`, `1`, `True`, `b\"list\"`, `\"dict\"`) return Arnio's normal `ValueError`, so the behavior is inconsistent.\n\n## Severity / impact\nLow. This is a validation-polish bug in a public export helper. It does not corrupt data, but it leaks implementation details and makes bad-input handling inconsistent.\n\n## Likely affected area\n- `arnio/frame.py::ArFrame.to_dict`\n- Tests for `orient` validation\n\n## Suggested next action\nValidate `orient` is a string before checking membership in the supported set, then raise a deliberate `TypeError` or the existing supported-values `ValueError`. Add regression tests for list and dict inputs.\n\n## Related but distinct\n#2410 tracks the published `1.19.0` wheel missing orient support. This issue is for the current-source invalid-input path after orient support is present.\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/2472",
 "pr": 2511,
 "pr_title": "fix: validate orient type in ArFrame.to_dict",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\r\n- Added an explicit `isinstance(orient, str)` type check in `ArFrame.to_dict()` before evaluating set membership to safely prevent raw Python `TypeError: unhashable type` leaks when users pass mutable objects like lists or dictionaries.\r\n- Preserved the existing `ValueError` contract for invalid/unsupported string inputs and maintained backward compatibility for all valid orientations.\r\n- Added comprehensive regression tests covering unhashable lists, unhashable dictionaries, hashable non-strings (integers), and invalid strings.\r\n\r\n## Linked issue\r\nFixes #2472\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n- [x] Bug fix\r\n- [ ] Feature\r\n- [ ] Performance improvement\r\n- [ ] Documentation\r\n- [x] Tests\r\n- [ ] Refactor\r\n- [ ] CI / packaging\r\n\r\n## Area\r\n- [ ] CSV parser / I/O\r\n- [ ] C++ cleaning engine\r\n- [x] Python API / ArFrame\r\n- [ ] Pipeline / custom steps\r\n- [ ] Data quality / profiling\r\n- [ ] Schema validation\r\n- [ ] pandas interoperability\r\n- [ ] Docs / website\r\n- [ ] Developer tooling\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\nRan focused pytest targeting the new regression tests along with formatting checks locally:\r\n```bash\r\npytest tests/test_frame.py -k test_to_dict_invalid_orient_types\r\npython -m ruff check --fix arnio/frame.py tests/test_frame.py\r\npython -m black arnio/frame.py tests/test_frame.py",
 "fix_commit": "7b2ed5a4fec3f146258d296d2b6ba39b8e5c7ac9",
